    "/internal/verification/identity-grant-token": {
      "get": {
        "description": "A PURPOSE-SCOPED, one-way uniqueness token for onboarding's once-per-verified-identity grants.\n\nonboarding needs a stable, deletion-surviving, cross-tenant key so a welcome grant issues once per\nreal person \u2014 but it must NEVER receive the claim_ref itself, because that stable hash would let it\ncorrelate the same person across tenants (the exact linkage the hashing hides). So this returns\nHMAC(PII_SALT, \"onboarding-grant|<claim_ref>\") instead: unique per verified identity (dedup works),\nstable (same person \u2192 same token, survives deletion like the claim_ref), but one-way and bound to\nTHIS purpose \u2014 it cannot be reversed to the claim_ref or matched against the claim_ref used\nanywhere else. Empty token when the subject has no VERIFIED verification of this identity claim,\nso a grant gated on it fails CLOSED (withheld, never issued on an unverified claim).",
        "operationId": "identity_grant_token_internal_verification_identity_grant_token_get",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "in": "query",
            "name": "tenant",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "title": "Tenant",
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          {
            "in": "query",
            "name": "subject",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "title": "Subject",
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          {
            "in": "query",
            "name": "claim_type",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "title": "Claim Type",
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          {
            "in": "header",
            "name": "X-Internal-Token",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                {
                  "type": "null"
                }
              ],
              "title": "X-Internal-Token"
            }
          },
          {
            "in": "header",
            "name": "X-Internal-Assertion",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                {
                  "type": "null"
                }
              ],
              "title": "X-Internal-Assertion"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "additionalProperties": true,
                  "title": "Response Identity Grant Token Internal Verification Identity Grant Token Get",
                  "type": "object"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful Response"
          },
          "422": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Validation Error"
          }
        },
        "summary": "Identity Grant Token",
        "tags": [
          "internal"
        ]
      }
    },
    "/internal/verification/identity/{claim_ref}/seen": {
      "get": {
        "description": "Has this verified identity been seen before?\n\nThe anti-abuse question, asked by onboarding-service before it grants anything once per\nidentity. Internal tier because the caller is a SERVICE, not a person \u2014 a capability check\nwould have been machine auth wearing a user's clothes.\n\nTakes a claim_ref rather than a raw value on purpose: the caller must already hold the hash, so\nthis cannot be used to ask whether a given national id exists in our records. A raw-value\nendpoint here would be an enumeration oracle over a national registry.",
