    "/internal/verification/resolve": {
      "post": {
        "description": "A provider's ASYNC callback: settle a PENDING verification the provider answered later.\n\nNafath-style providers push a prompt to a phone and answer minutes later \u2014 `pending` is a real\nverdict whose only legitimate way forward is this callback. Without a route wired to\nVerificationService.resolve(), a pending verification could ONLY ever lapse to EXPIRED via the\nsweep, so no async check could ever succeed (audit verification-02).\n\nInternal tier because the caller is the provider integration (a service), not a user. IDEMPOTENT:\nresolve() only moves a still-PENDING record, so a retried callback changes nothing. 404 when the\nid is unknown; 409 when it had already lapsed/settled (the returned verdict says which).",
        "operationId": "resolve_verification_internal_verification_resolve_post",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "in": "header",
            "name": "X-Internal-Token",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                {
